    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0213" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 793.94/242.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-26T19:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1915—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram of February 23, 8 p.m. At Sino-Japanese diplomatic conference
                    yesterday the opening of additional treaty ports in Shantung was agreed to. The
                    Chinese Government refused to accept the <pb facs="0214" n="98" xml:id="pg98"/>
                    wording of preamble of Article II that “the Chinese Government has always
                    acknowledged the special position enjoyed by Japan in South Manchuria and Inner
                    Mongolia” and they will continue to resist the attempt to have a special status
                    of Japan in that region formally sanctioned. Next meeting Sunday [the 28th].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
